From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:13:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: stop MXC sandboxes from moving the ancestors of
 protected paths

A writable root that contained a read-only or denied path let a sandboxed command rename or delete the directory
that holds that path and so replace it. The launcher now grants such an ancestor read-only and grants each of its
other children writable, so the protected path stays where it is while its siblings remain writable. Unreadable
ancestors are still left ungranted, and a protected path that does not exist yet does not guard its ancestors.
---
